{
  "info": {
    "name": "Kirowen API v0",
    "_postman_id": "4c0f6a52-8e1b-4f1e-9d6a-6b1f0d2a7c10",
    "description": "Requests for the Kirowen HTTP API (`docs/api-v0.md`) and the public log.\n\n**Order for a first run:** Info, then Register a source (signs the proof in the sandbox), then Me, Create object and Get object.\n\n**Production writes are permanent.** Registering a source appends a key-statement leaf to the public log and it is never removed. Registrations are limited to 5 per IP per hour. Point `baseUrl` at a local `kirowend` to experiment freely.\n\n**Events:** Postman cannot build a COSE_Sign1 envelope. Submit an envelope file (≤ 1 KiB) made with the CLI, or download one with Get envelope and resend it to test idempotency.\n\n**Secrets:** `token` and `sourceSeed` are kept as current values only. Do not export them or commit them.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
